  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Humanitarian Response to Crisis-Affected Populations in Hungary</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24 February 2022, the Russian Federation launched a broad military offensive against Ukraine, forcing people to look for safety in the neighbouring countries. Since the beginning of the full-scale invasion, more than 11 million of border crossings from Ukraine were recorded, Hungary being second after Poland in the number of crossings. The complexity of the overall situation requires humanitarian actors to respond to the needs of the most vulnerable displaced &#x2013; particularly female-headed households, children, persons with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses, as well as the elderly. With winter approaching, and the utility prices in Hungary increasing up to 10 times, many households who were coping with the cost of living during warm months, may struggle to survive.Through this project, IOM aims to protect and support those particularly vulnerable among women, children, persons with disabilities, and elderly persons displaced from Ukraine by (1) providing shelter; (2) distributing food and hygiene items; (3) establishing food banks; and (4) development of childcare facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
